{
  "_provenance": "Stufe5/Dokumentenaustausch/DocumentReference-Read.feature: 'A valid DocumentReference resource that is referenced as \"replaces\" must exist in the system under test, and its ID must be stored in the configuration variable documentreference-read-replaces-id.' That variable is defined in no testdata file in 2.7.0 and is referenced by no step, so the inventory - which is keyed off the contract - cannot list this resource; only the prose asks for it. The assertion that does run, relatesTo.where(code = 'replaces' and target.reference.exists()).exists(), needs the reference but not the target, so a missing target would still pass the read scenario while leaving the seed set referentially broken. Authored to ISiKDokumentenMetadaten because the precondition says 'valid', which for a DocumentReference in this module means profile-conformant, and IRIS $validate then checks that claim before the round starts.",
